<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for FeedsEngine.app, the process that hosts the Zoom Meeting SDK.

  NOT for the plugin bundle, and therefore not for OBS. Only the engine loads
  ZoomSDK.framework; the plugin reaches the engine over a socket. An entitlement
  a binary does not need is attack surface it should not carry, and this one in
  particular weakens a protection OBS should keep.

  WHY disable library validation. Library validation requires every library
  loaded into a process to be signed by the SAME Team ID as the process (or by
  Apple). ZoomSDK.framework arrives pre-signed by Zoom, and Feeds is signed by
  us, so the two Team IDs differ by construction and dyld refuses the load:

    Termination Reason: Namespace DYLD, Code 1 Library missing
    Library not loaded: @rpath/ZoomSDK.framework/Versions/A/ZoomSDK
    Reason: code signature not valid for use in process: mapping process and
            mapped file (non-platform) have different Team IDs

  That is the crash this file fixes. Apple's documented mechanism for an app
  that loads a bundled framework signed by another team is exactly this
  entitlement. Library validation is switched on by the hardened runtime, which
  the OBS plugin template enables for every non-Debug configuration (see
  cmake/macos/xcode.cmake), and which notarization will require later anyway.

  STYLE NOTE: no double hyphen anywhere in this comment. XML forbids it inside
  comments and Apple's entitlements parser enforces that strictly, failing the
  codesign call with a bare "syntax error near line N" that names this file and
  nothing else.

  Camera and microphone are deliberately NOT requested. Feeds joins with audio
  and video off and only receives other participants' media. If the SDK ever
  needs a local device, the entitlement AND the matching usage string in
  FeedsEngine-Info.plist have to be added together.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
